# Agent scope & isolation

Used with [docs/AGENT-LANES.md](../../docs/AGENT-LANES.md) and prompts in `.cursor/agents/`.

## Path lock

- Do not modify files outside the **Allowed paths** in the chat kickoff.
- Do not touch **Locked paths** (Main owns them this session).
- No drive-by refactors of adjacent business logic.

## Lane write targets

| Lane / agent | May write |
|--------------|-----------|
| Agent 1 QA | `tests/*.test.mjs`, optionally `scripts/test-*.mjs` / test wiring in `package.json` |
| Agent 2 Bug Hunter | Chat report; optionally `docs/audits/*.md` only |
| Agent 5 Docs Auditor | `docs/**` only |
| Main / Side feature | Production code inside Allowed paths for that ticket |

Audit and verification agents must not “fix while reporting” unless the user promotes them to a new Side ticket.

## Git

- One agent = one branch from latest `main` when writing (never share a long-lived agents branch).
- Do not merge or ship unless the user explicitly asks.
- Follow `git-pr-workflow.mdc` and `pr-size.mdc` (one concern per PR).

## Safety

- No `.env` or secrets in commits or reports (`security-secrets.mdc`).
- No PHI in logs, fixtures, or audit reports (`phi-handling.mdc`).
- Preserve intentional graceful degradation (`graceful-degradation.mdc`).

## Stop

If the task needs Locked paths, expands past one concern, or needs a product decision — stop and report.
